# AegisVPN fleet definition.
# Copy to deploy/fleet.conf and fill in YOUR VPS hosts.
#
# Format (one node per line):
#   name,host,role,country,city[,port]
#
#   name    node id shown in clients (must be unique in coord)
#   host    user@ip  for remote deploys over ssh (key auth, sudo),
#           or the literal "local" for a node deployed on this machine
#   role    standard | p2p | double-entry | double-exit | obfs
#   port    optional; defaults 51820 (exit nodes 51821)
#
# Double VPN chains: pair one double-entry with one double-exit in DIFFERENT
# jurisdictions. Clients connect to the entry; the relay service forwards
# entry subnet 10.8.0.0/24 -> the exit node's 10.8.1.0/24 (see server/relay).
#
# Coordination + shared secrets (also accepted as env):
#   AE_COORD_HOST=coord.example.com:8080
#   AE_COORD_TOKEN=<token printed by coord on first boot / set in server/.env>
#   AE_OBFS_KEY=<passphrase shared with obfsd>
#
# ── example fleet ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# # three standard exits
# us-east-1,root@203.0.113.10,standard,US,Ashburn
# de-fra-1,root@198.51.100.22,standard,DE,Frankfurt
# jp-tyo-1,root@192.0.2.77,standard,JP,Tokyo
#
# # one Double VPN chain across jurisdictions
# nl-ams-entry,root@203.0.113.50,double-entry,NL,Amsterdam
# ch-zrh-exit,root@198.51.100.90,double-exit,CH,Zurich
#
# # DPI-resistant obfuscated node (UDP masked on :443)
# se-sto-obfs,root@192.0.2.140,obfs,SE,Stockholm
#
# # P2P-optimized node (torrent-friendly, no logging of peer traffic)
# sg-p2p-1,root@198.51.100.201,p2p,SG,Singapore
